  "generationBrief": "Generate one horizontal six-pose walk row and one six-pose run row for each existing classic character. Preserve reference identity, clothing, blue hair dye channel, full body and transparency; alternate foot contacts and opposing arm swings. Minjae run was regenerated using his walk row to preserve the center-part bob instead of bangs. This is a summary of generation instructions, not an exact prompt transcript.",
  "pipeline": [
    "canonical sprite-gen prepare",
    "canonical sprite-gen component extraction",
    "canonical sprite-gen compose-atlas",
    "canonical sprite-gen inspect",
    "Pillow lossless WebP encoding with decoded RGBA pixel-equality verification"
  ],
  "exportPrep": "For each actor, canonical sprite-gen connected-component extraction measured all 12 source poses. One uniform scale per actor, min(288/max_component_width,368/max_component_height,1), was applied to every component in both rows before canonical extraction; components were bottom-centered in their original six-slot strip. Originals were copied to each run raw-original directory and SHA256 recorded in common-scale-prep.json.",
  "runtime": {
    "generatedCollections": [
      "classic/signature (plus any EXTRA_MOTION_SHEETS entry in app/lounge-rig-frames.ts)"
    ],
    "otherCollections": "Every other look walks and runs with the cut-out rig: scripts/build-lounge-rig.mjs segments each static atlas cell offline into torso, legs (thigh/shin) and forearms (app/lounge-rig-data.ts); app/lounge-rig.ts poses the dyed composite with 8 cached poses per cycle (app/lounge-gait.ts). Legacy original step frames are replaced by the rig while moving.",
    "frameLayout": "app/lounge-motion-layout.json",
    "walkClockFps": 8,
    "runClockFps": 9,
    "runDistanceMultiplier": 1.65,
    "scaling": "one actor-wide source scale and one runtime cycle crop",
    "load": "local classic motion prewarmed during 3D scene loading; other actors on first visible movement",
    "fallback": "cut-out rig while a hand-drawn sheet is pending or if it fails to load",
    "frameClock": "app/lounge-gait.ts GAIT_CYCLES_PER_PHASE (walk 8/6, run 9/6 cycles per locomotion phase unit); hand-drawn frames and rig poses share it"
  },
  "limitations": "Input illustrations contain some near-repeated poses and crouch/head-size variation. Extractor warnings are not motion-cycle validation; stride, foot contacts, and loop continuity are unverified.",
